# =============================================================================
# What a consumer actually receives when they install this package.
#
# A dbt Package Hub install does not clone this repository. The hub's registry
# entry carries a `downloads.tarball` URL pointing at GitHub's source tarball
# endpoint (https://codeload.github.com/<org>/<repo>/tar.gz/<tag>); dbt
# downloads that tarball and untars it straight into the consumer's
# dbt_packages/ directory. Those tarballs are `git archive` output, and
# `git archive` omits every path marked `export-ignore`. So anything listed
# below never lands in anyone else's project.
#
# This was verified, not assumed. Commands and output are in
# docs/INSTALL_FOOTPRINT.md.
#
# Two limits to know before editing this file:
#
#   - A `git:` install clones the repo, so it ignores export-ignore entirely
#     and delivers everything here. That is a real gap, but the README
#     recommends the hub install and hub installs are the large majority.
#
#   - Local development installs the package with `- local: ../`, which dbt
#     resolves to a *symlink* into the working tree. export-ignore cannot
#     affect a symlink, so nothing in this file can break integration_tests/.
#
# Rule of thumb: if dbt does not parse it and a licence does not require it,
# it does not ship.
# =============================================================================

# A complete dbt project that installs this package from `../`. The largest
# single exclusion and the one that grows fastest as the test suite fills in.
/integration_tests/  export-ignore

# CI workflows, issue templates, PR template, CODEOWNERS.
/.github/            export-ignore

# Working documents. Also the guard rail for generated dbt docs: never commit
# catalog.json, manifest.json or index.html to the default branch outside a
# path excluded here. Committed docs artifacts are the single biggest source
# of bloat in published packages (they are 69% of fivetran/dbt_hubspot).
/docs/               export-ignore

# Contributor-facing documentation. Someone debugging inside dbt_packages/
# needs README.md and CHANGELOG.md. They do not need our conventions file,
# our contribution guide, our decision log, or our release runbook.
/CLAUDE.md           export-ignore
/CONTRIBUTING.md     export-ignore
/DECISIONLOG.md      export-ignore
/RELEASE.md          export-ignore

# Repo plumbing that carries no meaning inside dbt_packages/.
/.gitattributes      export-ignore
/.gitignore          export-ignore

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Everything not listed above ships, deliberately:
#
#   dbt_project.yml, packages.yml    dbt parses them
#   models/ macros/ seeds/ tests/    the configured paths
#   snapshots/ analyses/
#   LICENSE                          Apache 2.0 requires the licence to
#                                    accompany distributions; non-negotiable
#   README.md                        the first thing read when debugging
#                                    inside dbt_packages/
#   CHANGELOG.md                     answers "which version am I on"
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
